  "notes": "Public/private roles of subnets cannot be tied to specific route tables in one leaf (no multi-hop), so routes are checked per gateway. Defaulting to all available AZs is checked as subnets referencing the aws_availability_zones data source or spanning 6 distinct AZs (AZ names not pinned); the variable that makes the count configurable is not named in the prompt and is not pinned. The GT declares no region variable; the region check reads the planned region of the VPC. Review 2026-09-24: route checks no longer pin the 0.0.0.0/0 destination (any route to the IGW/NAT). | 2026-10-03 review: region accepted as a variable default (plan carries no region attribute on this provider version); NAT routes accepted from declared route blocks."
